    <div class="field--name--field-intro">
      
<div class="field field--name--field-content field--type--entity-reference-revisions field--label--hidden node--view-mode--list">
  
          <div  class="field-content field-loop-count-1 field-first field-last">  <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--wysiwyg-text-with-media paragraph--view-mode--list">
          
<div class="field field--name--field-text-with-media field--type--text-long field--label--hidden">
    
      <div  class="field-text-with-media">  <div class="tex2jax_process"><p>Although both are sea waves, a tsunami and a tidal wave are two different and unrelated phenomena. A tidal wave is a shallow water wave caused by the gravitational interactions between the Sun, Moon, and Earth ("tidal wave" was used in earlier times to describe what we now call a tsunami.) A tsunami is an ocean wave triggered by large earthquakes that occur near or under the ocean, volcanic...</p></div>

